# Fixed defect 133's class, 2026-10-02 (lane recovery-b7, beside the
# audit's rows 133-m-const_alone and 133-m-fn_alone), a declaration's head
# that failed before its body, with no body below it. Symptom: `function`
# alone, `function f` with no list, `constant MAX` with no type, `test`
# with no name, `record` and `variant` with no name each told the head's
# mistake alone, and the missing body, fields or cases only once the head
# was mended: a turn per part, where `if n > )` over nothing and `function
# f() -> )` over nothing told both. Cause: a failed head dropped its line
# and read a block below it, and asked nothing where none stood. Now it is
# asked as under any head that refused something (`selfhost/parse/tails.hero`,
# `owed_body`; `selfhost/parse/members_below.hero`, `here_or_told`), and
# told at the next line, or at its head for a record or a variant. Beside
# it, and unchanged: over a body the body is read, never called absent
# (`fixedbugs-131-a-declaration-head-cut-short`); `constant MAX = 5` holds
# its value on its line, which is the head's one report.

#~v expected_name
function
function no_list  #~ missing_body expected_params
constant NO_TYPE  #~ missing_body expected_constant_type
test  #~ missing_body expected_test_name
record  #~ missing_body expected_name empty_record
variant  #~ expected_name empty_variant

constant INLINE = 5  #~ expected_constant_type

function main()
    print(1)

#~v expected_params
function at_the_end  #~v missing_body
